// `io.flush()` is nullary, and the checker arity-gates it like every other native.
//
// The bad call sits in a function nothing calls, and the program prints if it runs. That is what
// makes this case a check of the **checker**: a runtime arity check inside the dispatch raises the
// same code at the same span, so a case that simply called `io.flush(1)` at top level would stay
// green with the static rule gone. Here the only way to produce E0007 is to reject the program
// before it runs, and the only way to get the program's output is to have failed to.
// expect: error E0007 at 14:5
// expect: exit 1
use std.io

fn never_called(): void {
    // One argument to a 0-parameter function.
    io.flush(1)
}

echo "this program runs only if the call above was accepted"
